Table  1  presents the phases and chemical species included in this study. On the basis of local rate equations and specific reaction mechanisms, the chemical processes involve mass transfer across multiple phases and components, coupled with momentum and heat exchange [ 18 ,  25 ,  26 ,  27 – 28 ]. Table  2  summarizes the chemical reactions and phase transformations incorporated into the model. To implement the rate equations used for these reactions, the authors adapted and refined existing models and data available in literature [ 14 ,  17 ,  20 ,  29 ,  30 ,  31 ,  32 ,  33 – 34 ]. Interphase exchanges of energy and momentum are described on the basis of local flow conditions, composition, and temperature, using formulations derived from fundamental principles [ 21 ,  35 ,  36 ,  37 ,  38 – 39 ]. These formulations were subsequently adapted to reflect the specific operating conditions of the blast furnace and new burden materials [ 17 ,  20 ,  35 ,  40 ].
